  'help.econTitle': 'Economy', 'help.econ': 'Citizens gather Food (berries, hunting, farms), Wood (trees) and Gold (veins). Praying at a Temple yields <b>Favor</b> (for mythic creatures and heroes). Scholars at the Academy yield <b>Knowledge</b> (for research and Ages). Drop-off points (Granary, Lumber Camp, Mine) near resources speed up gathering. Each farm holds 1 citizen.',
  'help.bordersTitle': 'Borders and attrition (Rise of Nations style)', 'help.borders': 'Town Centers, Fortresses, Temples and Towers project borders. You can only build inside them (except new Town Centers on neutral land). Enemy troops inside your borders suffer continuous <b>attrition</b>. Research <b>Civics</b> at the Academy to expand borders and allow more Town Centers.',
  'help.combatTitle': 'Combat', 'help.combat': 'Infantry beats cavalry, cavalry beats archers, archers beat infantry. Siege brings down buildings. Heroes deal triple damage to mythic creatures; mythic creatures devastate humans. Garrison citizens and infantry in Town Centers, Fortresses and Towers to protect them (and fire extra arrows).',
